<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea's 1996 oil products exports up 30 pct - govt.</title>
<headline>S.Korea's 1996 oil products exports up 30 pct - govt.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's oil products exports grew 30 percent to 159.8 million barrels in 1996 against 122.8 million barrels a year before, the Ministry of Trade, Industry and Energy said on Thursday.</p>
<p>A ministry statement said growth in oil products output and a slowdown in domestic demand were responsible for the rise.</p>
<p>The nation's oil products imports rose 2.9 percent to 230.9 million barrels in 1996 from 224.5 million a year ago. The ministry did not give breakdown by product.</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5643</p>
</text>
